      "category": "just_cause_eviction",
      "title": "At-Fault Just Cause Termination Grounds",
      "requirement": "A landlord may terminate a tenancy for at-fault just cause only upon specified grounds: rent default, lease breach after notice, nuisance, waste, refusal to renew lease, criminal activity, criminal threats, unauthorized assignment/subletting, refusal of lawful landlord entry, unlawful use of premises, failure of an employee tenant to vacate after termination, or failure to vacate after giving written notice or surrender.",
